From 880a67f859e6f01bd0e40a8b3745fbaaa5052787 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:28:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/16] Principal model for human nodes (compromise D1): roles,
 delegation of authority, segregation of duties

src/principals.mjs, in OT-0's constitution vocabulary (roles; principals {id, kind, roles};
class ids like cust:*). IR (optional; old workflows unchanged, said in the schema): a
human node's principal {role, threshold?: {amount, above, role}} and the workflow's
segregation [{nodes}]. The role matrix is the host's (Foundry/Runtime option principals,
foundry answer --principals FILE --actor ID), never the workflow's or a model's.
Runtime: the requirement is bound when the question is asked (an amount above the
threshold, unreadable, or derived from untrusted data needs the threshold role); answers
are refused without a matrix, without an actor, from an unknown actor, without the roles,
or against a segregation rule (read from the hash chain, re-checked inside the CAS
update); human.answered records actor, roles and matrix hash. Validation: structure
always; with a matrix, the workflow satisfiability problem (PRINCIPAL_ROLE_UNHELD,
SOD_UNSATISFIABLE, SOD_UNSATISFIABLE_ABOVE_THRESHOLD) or a satisfying assignment.
principals.mjs joins the engine identity. docs/ARCHITECTURE.md describes it.
Tests: tests/principals.test.mjs 5/5 with constitution v1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011geBy7JvDqKuqhDyfmzd1U
